# Carry That Weight, bridge (figure 190.2): the opening section of "You Never Give Me Your Money"
# Sixteen bars (played twice on the record, first instrumental, then sung). Pollack's "d9 - 8" is
# the d chord with a 9-8 suspension, and "C4-3" a 4-3 suspension: each written as the chord with
# the figure, then the resolution on the second half of the bar.
# His "G13/11" (G with the 13th and 11th above it, the C triad in 6/4 position he mentions) is
# written C/G so it sounds as he describes; it resolves to G 5/3 in the last bar.
key a

